the Dark Kingdom of Obsidian.<br /> <br /> 2) Some Reckoning-type magic bullshittery went down<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;#2&quot; is also my assumption on the First Great Maelstrom, as that deposition of Emperor Romulus by Odoecar in 476 ce was NOT any kind of unprecedented catastrophe. It only ended up being significant later by the fact that no new Western Emperor ever rose again in Rome - which was more of a matter of gradual economic and organization decline (in favor of the &quot;Byzantine&quot; East) than anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T00:05:24-08:00","id":342696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/342514-does-the-book-of-oblivion-mean-we-ll-see-historical-settings?p=342635#post342635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently really curious as to how the Dark Kingdom of Obsidian was destroyed (setting off the Third Great Maelstrom). I mean, yes, smallpox was obliterating the indigenous population of the Americas, making European genocidal conquest easy - but in the Underworld that should have been SWELLING the Dark Kingdom's ranks, not weakening them against the Stygian Heretic colonists.<br /> <br /> So one of two things happened as far as I can see...<br /> <br /> 1) Stygian history got the order of events wrong - the smallpox devastation set off the Third Great Maelstrom (like the Black Death had the Second) via the massive amount of death - and the Maelstrom destroyed the Dark Kingdom of Obsidian.<br /> <br /> 2) Some Reckoning-type magic bullshittery went down<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;#2&quot; is also my assumption on the First Great Maelstrom, as that deposition of Emperor Romulus by Odoecar in 476 ce was NOT any kind of unprecedented catastrophe. It only ended up being significant later by the fact that no new Western Emperor ever rose again in Rome - which was more of a matter of gradual economic and organization decline (in favor of the &quot;Byzantine&quot; East) than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>We need to be clear on what's meant by the Dark Kingdom of Obsidian. In the context of the Third Great Maelstrom, it's referring to the Dark Kingdom that oversaw Mesoamerica, aka the Flayed Lands. (The Islands of Flint, which oversaw North America, simply withdrew to their islands in the Tempest in the face of the conquerers - revealed in, of all places, Mediums: Speakers with the Dead. The fate of the Lands of Gold, which oversaw South America, is unknown.)<br /> <br /> The Wraith Players Guide goes in-depth on the events that led to the Third Great Maelstrom. The Houses of the Flayed Lands couldn't agree about what to do about the invaders, whether to accept them or fight them, and so they were caught off-guard when the Heretics attacked. The Houses were powerful, and the fight was a long, bitter one, but they still couldn't unify in the face of the Stygian invaders, and the conquest of their Skinlands people (at this point the Aztec Empire) drained their power, leaving them vulnerable before the Heretics.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the First Great Maelstrom, Ends of Empire has a retcon. Charon had instituted a Tithe of the Dead, requiring two coins buried with the deceased. Those without the coins paid with their eyes or their hands. Many of those so maimed ended up in the Labyrinth, begging Oblivion for justice, and it came due in the fifth century AD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":".  Corrected Mediums' title 12-17-2014, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}